Source: @DISTRO_ID@-live
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: @DISTRO_HOME_URL@
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: @DISTRO_ID@-live
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, casper, mokutil, timeshift
Description: live session of the @DISTRO_NAME@ installation image
 Installed only in the squashfs of the installation ISO, never on an installed
 system (the installer removes it). It makes casper's live session land in the
 @DISTRO_NAME@ desktop: a casper-bottom script completes the SDDM autologin casper
 writes for the live user with the desktop's session name, and a boot test unit,
 inert unless the kernel command line carries @DISTRO_ID@.boottest, reports the
 live session's state on the serial console for the ISO boot test. Timeshift
 is in the live session to restore a btrfs install's snapshot when the
 installed system no longer starts; the installer keeps it on btrfs installs.
